  "articleBody": "Navigating permits for home lighting safety upgrades can feel a bit confusing, but it's really about ensuring your home is safe and up to code. Generally, if your project involves new wiring, adding new circuits, or making major additions to existing fixtures, you're likely going to need a permit and an inspection. This also applies to things like panel upgrades, work in bathrooms or kitchens, wet locations, or installing exterior lighting systems. Basically, if you're doing more than just swapping out a lightbulb or a simple plug-and-play fixture, it's worth looking into permit requirements. Ignoring permits for significant electrical work can lead to safety hazards and issues down the road, especially if you ever decide to sell your home. When in doubt, it's always best to check with your local Denver-area building department or chat with a qualified professional. They can help you understand the specific rules for your project and ensure everything is done correctly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}